 "result_text": "I changed `_get_data_format_3` in `ruuvitag_sensor/ruuvi.py` so it accepts format 3 data with the trailing NULLs trimmed. I haven't run it or any tests.\n\nThe old check required the raw hex string to be exactly 54 characters, which firmware 1.2.8 no longer sends. The new code accepts anything up to 54 characters that still has `03` at position 16. It then pads the string back to 54 with zeros before returning, so the decoder still gets the full 14 bytes it expects.\n\nI didn't touch the format 2/4 path because it searches for `ruu.vi/#` or `r/` in the data and doesn't depend on length. I also didn't do #29, the other change the issue mentions.",
